chasing power on eligible Indian brokerage platforms."},{"question":"What are the key moving average support and resistance levels for CORONA?","answer":"Based on daily technical charting, CORONA's short-term dynamic pullback support rests at its 20 EMA (\u20b92095.65), intermediate support at the 50 EMA (\u20b92081.93), and long-term institutional trend support at the 200 EMA (\u20b91818.28)."},{"question":"What are the daily pivot point support and resistance levels for CORONA?","answer":"For the current trading session, CORONA's central Pivot Point (PP) is \u20b92187.53. Immediate resistance levels are R1: \u20b92231.06 and R2: \u20b92280.93, while key downside support levels are S1: \u20b92137.66 and S2: \u20b92094.13."},{"question":"Which Indian broker provides the lowest MTF interest rate for CORONA?","answer":"Kotak Neo currently offers the lowest headline MTF interest rate starting at 9.69% p.a. (\u20b926.55/day per \u20b91 Lakh borrowed), followed by m.Stock at 9.99% p.a., Dhan at 12.49% p.a., and Zerodha at 14.60% p.a."},{"question":"At what price does CORONA trigger an MTF margin call or liquidation?","answer":"With a 25% initial margin, CORONA has a safety buffer of approximately 21.0%. If the price falls to \u20b91723.15, your broker will issue a margin shortfall notice. Positions must also be authorized via CDSL/NSDL OTP pledge before 9:00 PM on T-day."}],"last_updated":"2026-10-30T08:01:59.851622Z"}